 ersation\n\nThis event is a collaboration between the Consulate General of
  Brazil in San Francisco and Stanford University\, through its Program on 
 International and Cross-Cultural Education\, Global Studies Division\, Lan
 guage Center\, Abbasi Program in Islamic Studies\, Center for African Stud
 ies\, Department of Iberian and Latin American Cultures\, and Center for L
 atin American Studies.\n\nScreening of Antônio Pitanga's 2024 historical 
 film telling the homonymous 1835 uprising of enslaved Muslim workers in Sa
 lvador\, Bahia\, Brazil.\n\nA couple about to get married is kidnapped fro
 m their homeland in Africa and brought to Brazil as slaves. Separated by f
 ate\, they both struggle to survive the horrors of slavery and become invo
 lved in the largest Brazilian slave uprising.\n\nHors d'oeuvre and convers
 ation will follow the screening.
